window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-1177b242b3a05943"]={"key":"ny_main-1177b242b3a05943","group":"ny_main","uid":"1177b242b3a05943","rank":36,"title":"glassmere sunderly stateful margin review","occupation":"sales_managers","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are Iris Abara, the sales manager at Glassmere Fisheries, preparing material for Sunderly Media’s compliance reviewer. Ana Ferreira needs a revised client proposal and matching analysis workbook by 16:00 on Friday 12 September 2025 because the year-over-year margin comparison for Ontario and Michigan is being challenged, the supplied workbooks carry inconsistent dates, and the review has identified a segment for which a margin rate cannot currently be calculated. Work from `opening_state_2025.xlsx`, `event_ledger_2025.xlsx`, `margin_basis_memo.docx`, `plan_version_register.docx`, and `review_observations.docx`; these are the complete evidence bundle, so do not use the internet or introduce outside facts. Please produce one package in the top level of the working directory, using exactly the filename `sunderly_margin_review_package.zip`, and place inside it exactly `Sunderly_revised_proposal.pdf` and `Sunderly_reconciled_analysis.xlsx`. The workbook should contain tabs named `Reconciliation`, `Projection`, `Method`, and `Evidence`. (1) Reconcile the supplied opening position and subsequent account-plan events into an evidence-labeled comparison through the client presentation cutoff, showing the aligned source dates and the version basis used. (2) Present Ontario and Michigan separately as well as in any combined view you use, with the same comparison period, definitions, units, and treatment of exclusions so that a reviewer can tell whether an apparent difference is geographic or merely a timing or version artifact. (3) Show the relevant revenue, cost, margin, year-over-year movement, and any totals or rates needed to support the comparison; make the calculation basis and units visible rather than relying on unexplained displayed percentages. (4) Include a forward-looking projection under the scenarios or assumptions supplied in the evidence bundle, clearly separating projected figures from reconciled historical or current figures and identifying which inputs are sourced and which are assumptions. (5) Include a concise Method section that another analyst could use to reproduce the state reconciliation, explain how you handled the zero-denominator segment and other absent fields, and identify any source rows or fields that were deliberately excluded. (6) Use the Evidence tab and proposal PDF to label important figures with the source file, record or event reference, and calculation or assumption basis; the PDF should make the Ontario/Michigan comparison, aligned figures, zero-denominator convention, and factual implications easy for a compliance reviewer to verify. (7) Keep the proposal factual and bounded: it may describe observed patterns, variances, limitations, and implications for the presentation, but it must not recommend an action, invent a category, or present an unsupported explanation as fact. Do not silently repair, estimate, or overwrite evidence; if a value cannot be supported, show the treatment and its limitation. Keep the PDF suitable for client circulation, keep the workbook formulas or transparent calculation columns auditable, and ensure the final package opens cleanly without spreadsheet error strings.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/opening_state_2025.xlsx` — Opening account-plan state for the supplied comparison, including the prior-period reference measures and the current-period values that are changed by the event ledger.\n- `references/event_ledger_2025.xlsx` — Dated state-transition events for the account plan, including event attributes, row-level notes, a stale retired helper field, and one residual formula error that is not an authoritative input.\n- `references/margin_basis_memo.docx` — Client-issued basis memo defining the comparison measures, period boundary, treatment of a zero denominator, scenario inputs, and the supplied jurisdiction scope.\n- `references/plan_version_register.docx` — Register of account-plan versions with effective dates, preparation dates, and status information needed to resolve the workbook date mismatch.\n- `references/review_observations.docx` — Internal review observations from Ana Ferreira, Elena Fournier, Florian Hendricks, and Kwame Ellingsen identifying the questions the client reviewer expects the revised package to answer.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `sunderly_margin_review_package.zip` — A client-circulation package containing the revised evidence-labeled proposal PDF and the matching reconciled analysis workbook. (Write the ZIP file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly this filename.; The archive must contain exactly `Sunderly_revised_proposal.pdf` and `Sunderly_reconciled_analysis.xlsx` at its top level.; The workbook must contain tabs named exactly `Reconciliation`, `Projection`, `Method`, and `Evidence`.; The proposal must not recommend an action and must distinguish sourced facts, calculations, assumptions, projections, and limitations.; The workbook must be auditable offline and must not propagate spreadsheet error values or unsupported estimates.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/event_ledger_2025.xlsx","bytes":8150,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/46d25a71c0d8fc4e03dcc878263bbb1c5630f0654b1f3ec59c1305633d922020.xlsx","sha256":"46d25a71c0d8fc4e03dcc878263bbb1c5630f0654b1f3ec59c1305633d922020","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Change Ledger","row_count":19,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Glassmere Fisheries"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Account plan change ledger"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Exported","45905.47222222222"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Ledger entries"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Event Ref","Effective date","Plan version shown","Record Key","Event type","Revenue amount CAD","Cost amount CAD","Territory shown","Notes","Plan margin helper [retired]","Desk check"]},{"r":"7","cells":["E-2401","45853","GF-SM-25.2","P-ONT-410","Add","18500","13200","Ontario","","202000","=F7-G7  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"8","cells":["E-2402","45860","GF-SM-25.2","P-MI-510","Replace","678000","518000","Michigan","","156000","=F8-G8  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"9","cells":["E-2403","45871","GF-SM-25.2","P-ONT-427","Add","-8000","-6400","Ontario","Cancelled in client sign-off on 04-Aug-2025; exclude this ledger row from the account-plan state.","100000","=F9-G9  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"10","cells":["E-2404","45870","GF-SM-25.2","P-MI-523","Add","2500","0","Michigan","Jurisdiction correction: report P-MI-523 as Ontario from 01-Aug-2025; no revenue or cost adjustment.","77000","=F10/G10  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"11","cells":["E-2405","45905","GF-SM-25.2","P-MI-537","Add","12000","8640","Michigan","Effective date corrected to 28-Aug-2025 following signed amendment; apply 28-Aug-2025.","125000","=F11-G11  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"12","cells":["E-2406","45887","GF-SM-25.2","P-ONT-439","Add","9000","6400","Ontario","This change is for draft GF-SM-25.3 only; do not apply it to the approved GF-SM-25.2 state.","77000","=F12-G12  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"13","cells":["E-2407","45903","GF-SM-25.2","P-MI-549","Add","5000","4200","Michigan","","73000","=F13-G13  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"14","cells":["E-2408","45910","GF-SM-25.2","P-ONT-410","Replace","800000","600000","Ontario","","201000","=F14-G14  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"15","cells":["E-2409","45887","GF-SM-25.2","P-MI-510","Add","7000","4900","Michigan","","163000","=F15-G15  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"18","cells":["Trade Claims Queue - Great Lakes"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Claim ID","Supplier","Credit request CAD","Review owner","Received"]},{"r":"20","cells":["CLM-841","Pine Current Ice","1240","M. Laird","45901"]},{"r":"21","cells":["CLM-846","Westline Packaging","680","D. Chen","45902"]},{"r":"22","cells":["CLM-851","North Basin Transport","2150","M. Laird","45903"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/margin_basis_memo.docx","bytes":39452,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/56c238efa183ab1c8c4555be90952c35d3e765d15222a5f1f2513085d798c4c2.docx","sha256":"56c238efa183ab1c8c4555be90952c35d3e765d15222a5f1f2513085d798c4c2","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Margin comparison basis\nSunderly Media | issued 14 August 2025 | reference SM-25-14\nTo: Iris Abara, Glassmere Fisheries\nFrom: Ana Ferreira, Sunderly Media\nSubject: basis for the Ontario and Michigan annual account-plan margin comparison\nComparison boundary\nScope is Ontario and Michigan only. All amounts are CAD annual account-plan amounts. Compare the FY2024 approved annual plan measures in the opening extract with the FY2025 annual account-plan state after eligible changes through the presentation cutoff. The FY2025 figure is a state at the cutoff, not a later workbook-preparation date.\nParameter\nValue\nApplication\nPresentation cutoff\n31 Aug 2025, 17:00 ET\nApply eligible event states through this time.\nPrior comparison period\nFY2024 approved annual plan\nUse opening-extract prior revenue and cost; do not change them with ledger events.\nCurrent comparison period\nFY2025 annual plan state through cutoff\nStart with FY2025 opening amounts and replay qualifying events.\nPlan version selection\nLatest Approved Ontario & Michigan version effective on/before cutoff\nEffective date governs; preparation and workbook dates do not select a version.\nCurrency / units\nCAD / annual account-plan amounts\nNo conversion or annualisation is required.\n\nState and rate treatment\nReplay order. Use event effective date order. Add events add the revenue and cost amounts; Replace events supersede the current state with the revenue and cost amounts shown. An event is not applied outside the selected version, stated scope, or cutoff.\nMeasures. Margin dollars = revenue minus cost. Margin rate = margin dollars divided by revenue. Rate movement is shown in percentage points. Jurisdiction and combined rates must be calculated from summed eligible revenue and margin, never from an average of account rates.\nZero-denominator convention. Where revenue is zero, show the rate and rate movement as N/M. Retain the monetary values, but exclude that record from row-rate comparison and aggregate rate numerator and denominator. Do not infer a rate or a missing monetary amount.\nFY2026 scenario calculation\nThe following are supplied calculation assumptions, not observed results. For each row, calculate projected revenue as reconciled FY2025 revenue × (1 + scenario revenue change) + FY26 Rev overlay. Calculate projected cost as reconciled FY2025 cost × (1 + scenario cost change) + FY26 Cost input. Round projected monetary outputs to the nearest CAD.\nScenario\nRevenue change\nCost change\nFormula use\nScenario A - Measured carry-forward\n+2.5%\n+3.0%\nApply to reconciled FY2025 state, then add source overlay/input.\nScenario B - Cost variance\n+0.5%\n+4.5%\nApply to reconciled FY2025 state, then add source overlay/input.\n\nMissing forecast cost input. A blank FY26 Cost input is not zero. For that record, leave projected cost, margin, and rate blank; do not use an estimate or substitute. Projection totals and rates must identify that they use only records with both required forecast amounts.\nFor the presentation, state observed variances, source limitations, and calculation implications factually. This basis does not support a sales recommendation or causal explanation beyond the supplied records.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/opening_state_2025.xlsx","bytes":7455,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/324b0c1dadd6465a2f51026abbace881d01de8e7fe726e8f64fa7e800be782b2.xlsx","sha256":"324b0c1dadd6465a2f51026abbace881d01de8e7fe726e8f64fa7e800be782b2","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Plan Extract","row_count":16,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Glassmere Fisheries"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Account Plan Position Extract"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Opening state as at","45839.33333333334"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Workbook prepared","45903.38472222222"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Stated plan version","GF-SM-25.2"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Currency / plan basis","CAD / annual account-plan amounts"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Record Key","customer_name","Jurisdiction","Segment","Plan version","FY24 Revenue CAD","FY24 Cost CAD","FY25 opening revenue","FY25 opening cost","FY26 Rev overlay","FY26 Cost input"]},{"r":"9","cells":["P-ONT-410","Cedar & Row Foods","Ontario","Chilled retail","GF-SM-25.2","720000","547200","765000","578340","15500","12000"]},{"r":"10","cells":["P-ONT-427","Norell Banquet Supply","Ontario","Foodservice","GF-SM-25.2","438000","341640","455000","354900","9000","7200"]},{"r":"11","cells":["P-ONT-439","Orchard Lane Markets","Ontario","Independent grocer","GF-SM-25.2","295000","227150","312000","237120","6400","5120"]},{"r":"12","cells":["P-ONT-451","Bramble Square Events","Ontario","Seasonal allocation","GF-SM-25.2","72000","55200","0","0","0","0"]},{"r":"13","cells":["P-MI-510","Morrow Lake Grocers","Michigan","Chilled retail","GF-SM-25.2","650000","494000","680000","520000","14000","11200"]},{"r":"14","cells":["P-MI-523","Harbor Leaf Provisions","Michigan","Specialty counter","GF-SM-25.2","287000","220990","305000","233325","7300","5840"]},{"r":"15","cells":["P-MI-537","Beckett Cash Market","Michigan","Independent grocer","GF-SM-25.2","515000","396550","535000","409275","10500","8400"]},{"r":"16","cells":["P-MI-549","Strand Kitchen Supply","Michigan","Foodservice","GF-SM-25.2","336000","262080","350000","273000","8200",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Extract posted by Sales Operations; timestamps are retained from the export."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/plan_version_register.docx","bytes":38337,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/078fa053e04e903fd7f8779bffbd1af2647fe423a4c08c5c8f825a3b357bf5bc.docx","sha256":"078fa053e04e903fd7f8779bffbd1af2647fe423a4c08c5c8f825a3b357bf5bc","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Account plan version register\nGlassmere Fisheries | Sunderly Media account plan | prepared 03 September 2025\nThis register records plan filing status for the Ontario and Michigan account-plan set. Dates are retained from the filing record.\nVersion\nEffective date\nPrepared date\nStatus\nScope\nFiling note\nGF-SM-25.0\n01 Jan 2025\n18 Dec 2024\nArchived\nOntario & Michigan\nOpening annual framework\nGF-SM-25.1\n01 Apr 2025\n03 Apr 2025\nSuperseded\nOntario & Michigan\nSuperseded in July filing\nGF-SM-25.2\n01 Jul 2025\n14 Aug 2025\nApproved\nOntario & Michigan\nApproved state at issue\nGF-SM-25.3\n01 Sep 2025\n29 Aug 2025\nDraft\nOntario & Michigan\nDraft retained for review\nGF-SM-25.2-MI\n01 Jul 2025\n12 Aug 2025\nReference only\nMichigan\nLocal filing reference\n\nFiling note: The Sales Operations workbook export was generated after the opening-state timestamp; export and prepared dates are not effective dates.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/review_observations.docx","bytes":38483,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a37894259229dcfe117dee1c9a2ad386c289bed9384300c445cf9cbbd42f9075.docx","sha256":"a37894259229dcfe117dee1c9a2ad386c289bed9384300c445cf9cbbd42f9075","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Margin review observations\nSunderly Media account-plan comparison | internal review notes | 04 September 2025\nThe following notes were recorded while preparing the client-review materials. They identify matters to make visible in the revised comparison; they do not add quantitative source data.\nReviewer\nObservation\nIris Abara\nPlease identify the approved plan version by its effective date. The opening workbook appears to have been prepared later than the state it describes.\nElena Fournier\nOntario and Michigan should be shown side by side using the same annual plan measure, cutoff, currency, and rate convention.\nAna Ferreira\nThe line with no current revenue should not be represented by a percentage. Please show how it is treated in the total rate and identify the limitation.\nFlorian Hendricks\nThe state changes need record and event references. Notes in the ledger may matter more than the adjacent fields when they state a correction or cancellation.\nKwame Ellingsen\nKeep scenario calculations visibly separate from reconciled figures. The reviewer needs to see which source inputs are absent rather than an inferred amount.\n\nPresentation framing: describe observed patterns, variances, limitations, and their implications for the presentation without adding an action position or unsupported explanation.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/sunderly_margin_review_package.zip","bytes":28075,"extension":".zip","url":"assets/714136d9bd4b4b525648329a7ad1c7a10b8e7fe30a17db210f00d00400faa462.zip","sha256":"714136d9bd4b4b525648329a7ad1c7a10b8e7fe30a17db210f00d00400faa462","preview":{"kind":"unavailable","note":"此格式未做网页解析，原文件可下载。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a ZIP package named exactly `sunderly_margin_review_package.zip`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted filename and archive listing.","grader_hint":"Check the top-level submitted filename; award only for the exact requested spelling and extension."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The ZIP contains exactly `Sunderly_revised_proposal.pdf` and `Sunderly_reconciled_analysis.xlsx` at its top level, with no extra deliverables.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"ZIP directory listing.","grader_hint":"Inspect the archive without relying on visual rendering; reject nested or additional files."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains tabs named exactly `Reconciliation`, `Projection`, `Method`, and `Evidence`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook sheet metadata.","grader_hint":"Inspect workbook sheet names; do not infer them from visible headings."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reconciliation uses the supplied presentation cutoff and a single, explicitly identified period basis rather than mixing the opening-state date, workbook preparation date, and event dates without explanation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation date fields, Method tab, and Evidence tab references.","grader_hint":"Compare the dates in the output with the basis memo, version register, opening state, and events; verify that the selected cutoff and period are consistent and disclosed."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For each in-scope account-plan state, the reconciled values equal the supplied opening state after applying the applicable supplied events in effective-date order through the disclosed cutoff, with no event applied outside its valid scope.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation rows, event references, and independent replay from the supplied files.","grader_hint":"Replay the state transitions independently from the source records; compare monetary results within ±$1 and rates within ±0.1pp where applicable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every row-level exception expressed in the source `Notes` field is reflected in the output treatment, and the note takes precedence over conflicting ordinary event columns where the note states an exception.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Source Notes values, reconciliation treatment, and Method explanation.","grader_hint":"Inspect each non-empty exception note in the event ledger and verify the resulting inclusion, status, jurisdiction, or effective treatment rather than checking only aggregate totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The retired helper column does not determine any reported reconciliation, margin, comparison, or projection value; reported figures are reproducible from authoritative fields and stated calculations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Output formulas or calculation columns, Method tab, and independent recomputation from authoritative source fields.","grader_hint":"Recompute key figures while ignoring the helper column and confirm agreement within ±$1 or ±0.1pp; check that stale helper values are not copied into conclusions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The residual source formula error is treated as unusable evidence and is neither propagated into the workbook nor used to support a proposal statement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Source error location, output cells, formulas, and Method/Evidence disclosure.","grader_hint":"Trace the error-bearing source cell and confirm that no output formula references it and that the output explains the exclusion if relevant."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Ontario reconciled revenue, cost, margin dollars, and margin rate equal the corresponding independently replayed and filtered source-derived measures, within ±$1 for monetary values and ±0.1pp for the rate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation tab and independent source calculation.","grader_hint":"Calculate Ontario only from authoritative in-scope state rows after event replay; compare each displayed measure with the output."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Michigan reconciled revenue, cost, margin dollars, and margin rate equal the corresponding independently replayed and filtered source-derived measures, within ±$1 for monetary values and ±0.1pp for the rate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation tab and independent source calculation.","grader_hint":"Calculate Michigan using the same basis as Ontario and compare each displayed measure."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Ontario and Michigan comparison is like-for-like: the jurisdictions use the same period, metric definitions, event treatment, scope, and denominator convention, with any jurisdiction-specific source fact clearly identified rather than silently changing the method.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation tab, Method tab, and proposal comparison text.","grader_hint":"Check definitions and filters side by side; award only if any difference in treatment is sourced and disclosed."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For every included row, margin dollars and margin rate follow the definitions in the supplied basis memo, and displayed totals reconcile to their component rows within ±$1 and ±0.1pp where rates are shown.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook formulas or transparent calculation columns and basis memo.","grader_hint":"Recompute row and aggregate formulas from displayed source measures; do not accept a copied or unexplained rate."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Combined totals equal the sum of the included Ontario and Michigan components without double-counting accounts, events, or jurisdictions; weighted rates are not simple averages unless the output explicitly demonstrates that the weights make them equivalent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation totals and component rows.","grader_hint":"Independently sum the jurisdiction components and recompute the combined rate; use ±$1 and ±0.1pp tolerances."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The zero-denominator segment follows the convention in the supplied basis memo, the convention is stated in the Method tab and proposal, and the segment does not distort aggregate margin-rate calculations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Zero-denominator source rows, Method tab, proposal text, and aggregate formulas.","grader_hint":"Verify both the stated convention and its implementation; accept only a consistent treatment matching the governing memo, with rate comparisons within ±0.1pp."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Absent source fields are not silently estimated: the output identifies the affected records or fields and states the bounded assumption or exclusion used for each material result.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Method tab, Evidence tab, and affected reconciliation or projection rows.","grader_hint":"Compare blank source fields with output treatments and verify that every material gap has an explicit, internally consistent disclosure."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Projection outputs for each supplied scenario are calculated from the reconciled starting state and the scenario inputs in the basis memo, with monetary projections within ±$1 and projected rates within ±0.1pp of an independent calculation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Projection tab, scenario assumptions, and independent replay/calculation.","grader_hint":"Recompute each scenario from the output's stated starting values and the memo inputs; reject projections based on stale helper values or unsupported rates."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Historical or reconciled figures and forward projections are visibly separated and labeled so that a reviewer cannot mistake a scenario result for an observed result.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook labels, proposal labels, and scenario metadata.","grader_hint":"Inspect headings, legends, and narrative captions in both files; labels must be unambiguous without oral explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each material total, variance, jurisdiction comparison, and projection can be traced to a source file and record or to a transparent calculation chain documented in the Evidence tab.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Evidence tab citations and proposal figure labels.","grader_hint":"Sample key figures from both jurisdictions, the combined total, the zero-denominator treatment, and each scenario; follow citations back to supplied records."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal and workbook agree on all reported jurisdiction figures, totals, zero-denominator treatment, scenario results, and material scope qualifications within ±$1 for monetary values and ±0.1pp for rates.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Cross-document comparison of PDF text/tables and workbook values.","grader_hint":"Extract the PDF tables or text and compare them with workbook outputs; treat any unexplained discrepancy as a failure."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Method and Evidence material is sufficient for another analyst to reproduce the state replay and understand the handling of dates, notes, missing fields, the retired helper, the residual error, and the zero-denominator segment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Method and Evidence tabs plus the proposal's methodology note.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the disclosures identify decisions and source trails clearly enough for independent re-performance, not merely whether a method label exists."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal is suitable for a compliance reviewer: it presents factual implications and limitations plainly, distinguishes evidence from interpretation, and contains no recommendation or persuasive call to action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered proposal PDF and its extracted text.","grader_hint":"Review the document as a regulator or auditor would; unsupported causal claims, sales persuasion, or recommendations should lose this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Neither deliverable contains `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, or `#VALUE!` in visible text, formulas, cached values, or extracted PDF text.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Spreadsheet formula/value scan and PDF text extraction.","grader_hint":"Inspect both nested files programmatically and, where possible, render the workbook before scanning displayed values."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Penalty: any row from the unrelated adjacent table in the event workbook is treated as an account-plan event, state record, jurisdiction result, or projection input.","weight":-5.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Output record identifiers and independent comparison with the unrelated source table.","grader_hint":"Identify source rows belonging to the unrelated table and check whether any entered the output population or calculations."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Penalty: a projection-margin field for a source record whose forecast cost input is absent is populated with a numeric estimate or invented substitute rather than left blank or given the disclosed non-value treatment.","weight":-4.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Source missing-field marker and corresponding Projection or Reconciliation cells.","grader_hint":"Check the specifically affected records; do not penalize a clearly labeled non-numeric treatment that is consistent with the Method disclosure."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Penalty: the package adds unsupported accounts, categories, causal explanations, or jurisdictional facts that cannot be traced to the supplied files or transparent calculations.","weight":-4.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"All output populations and narrative claims compared with the supplied corpus.","grader_hint":"Look for invented entities, categories, explanations, or quantitative claims; apply once per substantive unsupported addition, capped at the item weight."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Iris Abara is the sales manager responsible for preparing a defensible client-facing comparison for Glassmere Fisheries and Sunderly Media. The package will be reviewed by compliance personnel before a client presentation, so traceability and bounded factual language matter more than persuasive sales framing.","difficulty_sources":["Stateful replay of an opening account-plan state through dated events","Resolving version timing from supplied effective-date evidence rather than workbook recency","Interpreting row-level free-text exceptions over conflicting main columns","Separating the unrelated adjacent table from the authoritative event population","Applying and documenting the supplied zero-denominator and missing-field conventions","Keeping projections, evidence labels, and factual implications consistent across a PDF and workbook"],"authoring_plan":{"mode":"stateful","source_count":5,"construction":"Build a small but realistic evidence dossier for a wholesale account-plan margin review. The authoritative answer must be generated by an offline reference script that loads the opening state, applies valid event transitions in effective-date order, selects the governing plan version, calculates the comparison measures, and then calculates the supplied forward scenarios. Do not hand-write gold outputs; derive every expected amount, rate, inclusion flag, and citation target from the source data.","governing_basis":{"file":"margin_basis_memo.docx","semantics":["Define the current and prior comparison periods and the presentation cutoff used for the review.","Define revenue, cost, margin dollars, and margin-rate formulas, including units and aggregation rules.","State the deterministic rule for selecting the plan version when effective date and preparation or workbook date disagree.","State the zero-denominator convention for the segment with no usable denominator.","Provide two clearly named forward scenarios with deterministic input assumptions and identify which missing forecast inputs cannot be substituted.","Limit the analysis to Ontario and Michigan and require factual implications rather than a recommendation."],"design_note":"This is a genuine client-issued basis memo, not a hidden answer key. It gives explicit deterministic rules so the main difficulty is source reconciliation and evidence handling."},"sources":{"opening_state_2025.xlsx":{"role":"Opening state","semantics":["Contains authoritative prior-period comparison measures and current-period opening measures for synthetic account-plan records in Ontario and Michigan.","Contains stable record keys, account and jurisdiction fields, revenue and cost measures, and the opening as-of metadata.","Include a small number of absent optional fields relevant to projection disclosure, but keep the authoritative historical measures complete except for the required zero-denominator case.","Do not include duplicate records, unit-conversion traps, or unrelated formula defects in this source."]},"event_ledger_2025.xlsx":{"role":"State transitions","semantics":["Contains dated account-plan events that change the current state, with authoritative event fields and effective dates.","Include events before and after the presentation cutoff so the reference replay must respect the governing period boundary.","Include row-level free-text Notes exceptions that conflict with ordinary columns; the notes must state concrete exceptions such as cancellation, reclassification, or an effective-date correction and must override the ordinary columns for those rows.","Include one retired helper column with stale values that disagree with values recomputed from authoritative fields; label it as retired in the source but do not explain its values in a solver-facing purpose.","Include exactly one residual formula error in a non-authoritative source cell. It must be safe to ignore and must not be needed for any authoritative result.","Include a nearby, clearly separate unrelated table with plausible text and numeric rows so that careless range selection could absorb it. This is a decoy structure rather than an additional account-plan source.","Do not seed duplicate rows, floating-point noise, packaging/unit traps, or any other standard defect."]},"plan_version_register.docx":{"role":"Version evidence","semantics":["Lists several synthetic plan versions with effective dates, preparation dates, status, and jurisdiction or scope labels.","Make at least one workbook date disagree with the effective version date and include a later or draft-looking entry that should be resolved under the basis memo rather than selected by recency alone.","All dates and statuses must be internally coherent under the memo's stated selection rule."]},"review_observations.docx":{"role":"Review trail","semantics":["Contains comments attributed only to Iris Abara, Elena Fournier, Ana Ferreira, Florian Hendricks, and Kwame Ellingsen.","Call out the requested alignment of Ontario and Michigan, the date mismatch, the zero-denominator segment, source traceability, and the need to distinguish factual implication from recommendation.","Do not put answer totals or hidden grading language in this file."]}},"defect_calibration":["Use exactly the three requested seeded layout defects: one stale retired helper column, one free-text Notes column with per-row overrides, and one residual formula error that must be ignored.","The adjacent unrelated table is required as a contextual decoy; do not add any other standard data-quality defect.","Choose fresh synthetic monetary amounts, rates, record keys, and scenario inputs that do not copy literal values from the prompt. Keep all identities and records synthetic and internally consistent."],"gold_derivation":{"script_steps":["Parse the authoritative opening-state records and freeze prior-period measures.","Read the version register and apply the basis-memo selection rule to identify the valid plan version at the cutoff.","Replay only valid in-scope events through the cutoff, allowing each qualifying Notes exception to override conflicting ordinary fields.","Ignore the retired helper and the residual formula-error cell completely.","Exclude the unrelated adjacent table from the account-plan population.","Calculate jurisdiction and combined revenue, cost, margin dollars, and rates; apply the memo's zero-denominator rule and preserve the required blank treatment for the record with missing forecast cost.","Calculate both forward scenarios from the reconciled starting state and memo inputs.","Use the resulting tables and source references to test the rubric relationally, including cross-deliverable agreement and error-string hygiene."],"gold_policy":"The reference solution is considered passed only when an independently generated package satisfies every positive predicate, does not incur any penalty, and remains understandable after offline extraction and rendering."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_opening_state","filename":"opening_state_2025.xlsx","purpose":"Opening account-plan state for the supplied comparison, including the prior-period reference measures and the current-period values that are changed by the event ledger.","required":true,"discovery":"Use as a supplied workbook attachment; inspect the labeled account-plan table and its stated as-of information."},{"artifact_id":"ref_event_ledger","filename":"event_ledger_2025.xlsx","purpose":"Dated state-transition events for the account plan, including event attributes, row-level notes, a stale retired helper field, and one residual formula error that is not an authoritative input.","required":true,"discovery":"Use as a supplied workbook attachment; distinguish the account-plan event table from the nearby unrelated table."},{"artifact_id":"ref_margin_basis","filename":"margin_basis_memo.docx","purpose":"Client-issued basis memo defining the comparison measures, period boundary, treatment of a zero denominator, scenario inputs, and the supplied jurisdiction scope.","required":true,"discovery":"Use as a supplied policy or basis document; its definitions govern the requested analysis."},{"artifact_id":"ref_version_register","filename":"plan_version_register.docx","purpose":"Register of account-plan versions with effective dates, preparation dates, and status information needed to resolve the workbook date mismatch.","required":true,"discovery":"Use as a supplied register; compare its version facts with the workbook metadata and event dates."},{"artifact_id":"ref_review_observations","filename":"review_observations.docx","purpose":"Internal review observations from Ana Ferreira, Elena Fournier, Florian Hendricks, and Kwame Ellingsen identifying the questions the client reviewer expects the revised package to answer.","required":true,"discovery":"Use as supplied review correspondence; treat observations as prompts for evidence and disclosure, not as additional quantitative data."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"del_margin_review_package","filename":"sunderly_margin_review_package.zip","media_type":"application/zip","description":"A client-circulation package containing the revised evidence-labeled proposal PDF and the matching reconciled analysis workbook.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the ZIP file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly this filename.","The archive must contain exactly `Sunderly_revised_proposal.pdf` and `Sunderly_reconciled_analysis.xlsx` at its top level.","The workbook must contain tabs named exactly `Reconciliation`, `Projection`, `Method`, and `Evidence`.","The proposal must not recommend an action and must distinguish sourced facts, calculations, assumptions, projections, and limitations.","The workbook must be auditable offline and must not propagate spreadsheet error values or unsupported estimates."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"analyze_data","work_product":"analytical_model","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"sales_managers","sector":"wholesale_trade","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":5.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent reviewer inspect the generated reference package against the supplied corpus and rubric, with a second pass focused on state replay, exception notes, date alignment, and cross-deliverable agreement.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The analysis is intentionally bounded to the synthetic evidence bundle and the jurisdiction and policy text supplied with it.","Visual review of PDF readability is necessary in addition to numeric replay because traceability and factual framing are partly professional judgments."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":false,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:51:45+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:51:45+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:51:45+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"gold-del_margin_review_package: rendering validation is not implemented for .zip","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:51:45+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/1177b242b3a05943","declared_deliverables":["sunderly_margin_review_package.zip"]};
